[Term]
id: HP:0030884
name: Gastrojejunal tube feeding in infancy
def: "Feeding problem necessitating gastrojejunal tube feeding." [PMID:11827911]
comment: The rationale for gastrojejunal tube feeding is that placing the tip of the tube beyond the ligament of Treitz prevented duodenogastric reflux or gastro-esophageal reflux. Gastrojejunal feeding tubes have since been used in children who are deemed too unfit for antireflux surgery or where fundoplication has failed.
synonym: "Gastro-jejunal tube feeding in infancy" EXACT []
