[Term]
id: PROMOT:0032012
name: Debilidad fatigable de la musculatura facial
def: "A type of weakness of the facial musculature (i.e. one or more muscles innervated by the seventh cranial nerve) that occurs after a muscle group is used and lessens if the muscle group has some rest. That is, there is diminution of the strength of the facial musculature with repetitive muscle actions." [] {IAO:0000119="HP:0003473"}
is_a: HP:0003473 ! Fatigable weakness
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string
property_value: PROMOT:1000001 "Congenital myasthenic syndrom Scoping review" xsd:string
property_value: PROMOT:1000001 "Congenital myopathy Scoping review" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0032013
name: Debilidad fatigable de los músculos oculares
def: "A type of weakness of the ocular muscles that occurs after a muscle group is used and lessens if the muscle group has some rest. That is, there is diminution of the strength of the ocular muscles with repetitive muscle actions." [] {IAO:0000119="HP:0003473"}
is_a: HP:0003473 ! Fatigable weakness
