[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100007
name: Assessment using Dysphagimeter
def: "An assessment that uses the Dysphagimeter scale to assess dysphagia or swallowing impairements. The Dysphagimeter is a patient-reported questionnaire that measures the ability to swallow foods of different textures and the impact of dysphagia on activities and participation. This questionnaire has three parts. Part A includes 24 items concerning solid foods, Part B includes 3 items on liquids and Part C includes 8 items, namely 6 items on the impact of dysphagia at meal times and 2 items on discomfort related to thick saliva. Each item offers 5 choices of descriptive answers. Parts A and B also include an option 'I cannot answer'. The participant must carefully read the instructions and check the answer that best corresponds to their situation for each item." [] {IAO:0000119="Definition translated from French to English using Reverso."}
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0002068 ! assesses Neuromuscular dysphagia
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0200136 ! assesses Oral-pharyngeal dysphagia

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100008
name: Assessment of pinch strengh using B & L gauge
def: "An evaluation procedure that uses a B&L gauge to assess pinch strengh. The test measuring the force of the lateral clamps, between the thumb and the index finger, allows quantifying the maximum voluntary strength of the hand and forearm muscles during a pinching action. This is an indicator of the level of hand function." [] {IAO:0000119="Definition translated from French to English from a Reverso’s suggestion."}
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0003392 ! assesses First dorsal interossei muscle weakness

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100009
name: Assessment of the maximum isometric muscle strength using MedUP dynamometer
def: "Assessment of the maximum isometric muscle strength of flexor and extensor muscles using MedUP dynamometer. It assesses the maximum isometric muscle strength in upper and lower limbs." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)"}
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0003547 ! assesses Shoulder girdle muscle weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0003694 ! assesses Late-onset proximal muscle weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0003731 ! assesses Quadriceps muscle weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0003810 ! assesses Late-onset distal muscle weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0008997 ! assesses Proximal upper limb muscle weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0009063 ! assesses Progressive distal muscle weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0009073 ! assesses Progressive proximal muscle weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0012515 ! assesses Hip flexor weakness

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100010
name: Assessment of tongue strengh using Iowa Oral Performance Instrument
def: "Assessment of the strengh of the tongue muscle by using Iowa Oral Performance Instrument." []
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0000183 ! assesses Tongue muscle weakness

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100011
name: Assessment using Berg Balance Scale
def: "An assessment with the Berg scale assesses balance and identifies the level of fall risk. This five-level ordinal scale (0 to 4) contains 14 items and the maximum total score ranges from 0 (maximum reach) to 56 (no reach detected). This generic scale evaluates various dimensions of balance, including the following: maintaining multiple positions, having automatic postural responses when changing posture or voluntary movements of the limbs, and produce effective balance and protection reactions." [] {IAO:0000119="Automatically translated from French."}
is_a: SNOMED:840297006 ! Assessment of patient reported outcome measures
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0002141 ! assesses Gait imbalance

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100012
name: 10 Meter Walk Test (10MWT)
def: "Le 10mwt est un test de capacité qui permet d’évaluer la vitesse de marche sur une courte distance pour deux conditions différentes, soit à la vitesse confortable et à la vitesse maximale. Le temps requis pour parcourir 10 mètres à la marche d’abord à la vitesse confortable, puis à la vitesse maximale, est inscrit." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
xref: http://snomed.info/id/431527001
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0002317 ! assesses Unsteady gait
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0002505 ! assesses Loss of ambulation

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100013
name: Assessment using Sydney Swallow Questionnaire (SSQ)
def: "Le questionnaire sur la déglutition de Sydney est un questionnaire auto-rapporté qui a pour but d’évaluer la gravité des problèmes de déglutition. Il comporte 17 questions. Le participant répond aux questions 1 à 11 et 13 à 17 en traçant un X sur une ligne (questions de type échelle visuelle analogue) et à la question 12 en cochant la réponse de son choix parmi 6 options. Une version canadienne-française validée a été créée." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
is_a: SNOMED:840297006 ! Assessment of patient reported outcome measures

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100014
name: 80 ml water swallowing test
def: "L’objectif de ce test est de boire 80 ml d’eau le plus rapidement possible sans s’étouffer. L’évaluateur déclanche le chronomètre quand les lèvres du participant touchent l’eau et l’arrête quand le participant dit « STOP »." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0002068 ! assesses Neuromuscular dysphagia
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0200136 ! assesses Oral-pharyngeal dysphagia

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100015
name: Assessment using Fatigue Severity Scale (FSS)
def: "Assessment using Fatigue Severity scale. It follows a 9-item scale which measures the severity of fatigue and its effect on a person's activities and lifestyle in patients with a variety of disorders.  A 9-item questionnaire with questions related to how fatigue interferes with certain activities and rates its severity according to a self-report scale. The items are scored on a 7 point scale with 1 = strongly disagree and 7= strongly agree. The minimum score = 9 and maximum score possible = 63. Higher the score = greater fatigue severity. Another way of scoring: mean of all the scores with minimum score being 1 and maximum score being 7. Lerdal (2011) found that items 1 and 2 in the FSS-9 should not be used in a mean score because the FSS-7 shows better validity and reliability and is likely more sensitive for measuring change in fatigue." [] {IAO:0000119="Source for the definition of the scale: https://www.sralab.org/rehabilitation-measures/fatigue-severity-scale"}
comment: Krupp, L. B., LaRocca, N. G., Muir-Nash, J., & Steinberg, A. D. (1989). The fatigue severity scale. Application to patients with multiple sclerosis and systemic lupus erythematosus. Archives of Neurology, 46(10), 1121–1123. 
is_a: SNOMED:840297006 ! Assessment of patient reported outcome measures
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0012378 ! assesses Fatigue

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100016
name: Assessment using Hand Jamar dynanometer
def: "Le test mesurant la force de préhension permet de quantifier la force maximale volontaire des muscles de la main et de l’avant-bras, lors d’une action de flexion des doigts. Il s’agit d’un indicateur du niveau de fonction de la main." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
xref: http://snomed.info/id/445993006
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0009005 ! assesses Weakness of the intrinsic hand muscles
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0031177 ! assesses Finger flexor weakness
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0033466 ! assesses Weak grip

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0100017
name: Stair Climb Test
def: "Le test de 10 marches évalue la capacité à monter et descendre un bloc de 10 marches pour deux conditions différentes, soit à la vitesse confortable et à la vitesse maximale. Ce test s’adressent aux participants qui ont la capacité d’utiliser les escaliers." [] {IAO:0000119="Definititon of the test provided by the Groupe de Recherche Interdisciplinaire sur les Maladies Neuromusculaires (GRIMN)."}
xref: http://snomed.info/id/252482003
is_a: SNOMED:12894003 ! Functional assessment
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0003551 ! assesses Difficulty climbing stairs
relationship: PROMOT:2000002 HP:0033235 ! assesses Difficulty descending stairs

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0110001
name: Actividad
def: "Actividad es la realización de una tarea o acción por parte de una persona. Las limitaciones en la actividad son dificultades que una persona puede tener para realizar una tarea o acción." [] {IAO:0000119="Clasificación Internacional del Funcionamiento, de la Discapacidad y de la Salud"}
is_a: BFO:0000015 ! process
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string
property_value: seeAlso ICF:1394728112

[Term]
id: PROMOT:0120002
name: Participación
def: "A participation is an involvement in a life situation. Participation restrictions are problems an individual may experience in involvement in life situations" [] {IAO:0000119="International Classification of Functioning, Disability and Health (ICF)"}
is_a: BFO:0000015 ! process
property_value: IAO:0000117 "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5160-7927" xsd:string
